revious":"10:18:52","deltaSeconds":-914}}},"historicalRank":{"fieldSizeRank":10,"finishersRank":6,"finishRateRank":87,"winningTimeRank":1,"winningTimeRankDir":1,"totalRaces":98},"recordContext":{"menRecords":["overall"],"menPreviousRecord":{"time":"05:18:19","holder":"David GATEBE","year":2016,"type":"overall"},"heroicSecond":{"name":"Piet WIERSMA","time":"05:14:01","athleteId":"D5B1F1FB-04DE-40E4-9522-A3110550F5A0","brokenRecord":{"time":"05:18:19","holder":"David GATEBE","year":2016,"type":"overall"}},"womenRecords":["overall"],"womenPreviousRecord":{"time":"05:54:43","holder":"Frith VAN DER MERWE","year":1989,"type":"overall"},"womenWouldHaveWonMen":{"mostRecentYear":1992,"mensWinner":"Jetman MSUTHU","mensTime":"05:46:11"}},"narrative":"The 2023 Comrades Marathon was the 96th running of the race, run in the 'down' direction from Pietermaritzburg to Durban over 87.701 kms. The race was held on Sunday, 11 June. Conditions: Sunny and mild all day. Runners had 12 hours to complete the course.\n\nTete DIJANA claimed the men's title in 05:13:58, ahead of Piet WIERSMA (05:14:01) and Edward MOTHIBI (05:17:34). Gerda STEYN won the women's race in 05:44:54, followed by Adele BROODRYK (05:56:26).\n\nTete DIJANA's 05:13:58 set a new course record, beating David GATEBE's 05:18:19 from 2016. Gerda STEYN set a new women's course record of 05:44:54, surpassing Frith VAN DER MERWE's 05:54:43 from 1989. Remarkably, runner-up Piet WIERSMA's 05:14:01 also beat the previous record of 05:18:19 — a rare feat in Comrades history. Gerda STEYN's 05:44:54 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1992 (Jetman MSUTHU, 05:46:11).\n\nFrom a field of 20,547 entries, 14,897 runners crossed the finish line (72.5% completion rate), with athletes representing over 19 countries. The field comprised 11,944 men and 2,952 women (19.8% female). The average finish time was 10:03:38.\n\nMedals awarded: 20 Gold, 47 Wally Hayward, 836 Silver, 5,637 Bill Rowan, 4,189 Bronze, 4,168 Vic Clapham. 3,786 runners (25.4%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Tebello SKASA in 11:58:59.\n\nThis edition featured the 1st fastest winning time on record. Compared to the previous down run in 2022, the field was 28.5% larger.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 69% of the finishers, with 4,597 seniors (avg 09:45:47) and 10,299 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":100.0}